==Galician==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|gl|roa-opt|esquina}} (attested in the Galician ''{{w|Cantigas de Santa Maria}}'' c. 1264) perhaps from {{der|gl|got|*𐍃𐌺𐌹𐌽𐌰}},<ref>{{R:DCECH}}</ref> from {{der|gl|gem-pro|*skinō|t=rim, plate}}. Cognate with {{cog|fr|échine|t=spine of an animal}} and {{cog|en|shin}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gl|/esˈkina̝/}}

===Noun===
{{gl-noun|f}}

# [[corner]]
#* '''1432''', X. Ferro Couselo (ed.), ''A vida e a fala dos devanceiros''. Vigo: Galaxia, page 89:
#*: ''estando y Martín Peres de Trella fasendo hua parede á '''esquina''' da parede de hua sua casa''
#*:: Being there Martin Perez de Trella, who was building a wall next to the '''corner''' of the wall of a house that belongs to him
# [[edge]]

===Synonyms===
* {{l|gl|canto}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|gl
|esquinado
|esquinal
|esquinar}}

